anacrolix's NewDefaultClientConfig sets ListenPort=42069, so any client whose port isn't explicitly set silently pins to it. The pool only overrode ListenPort on a successful claim, leaving the ephemeral-fallback and no-range paths on 42069 -- the exact collision the pool was built to prevent, surfacing as a crashed background process (error only in log.txt). Resetting to 0 up front makes 'OS-assigned' the default and the pool port the explicit override, rather than relying on every branch to remember to set it. The same default also affects the add-flow scratch clients (preview.go, metadata.go); a ListenPort=0 fix there was drafted but deliberately left out of this commit.
